  "selection": "All saved same-class car Lost rows on46 other videos with at least2 free high-confidence candidates at unchanged forwardIoU>=0.2, age<=6 and at least one native first-public candidate. The517 singleton events have already been audited and are not relabelled. Unannotated queries and ambiguous GT remain explicit.",
  "reference": "Latest earlier annotation-timestamp with a real public native old-track observation, no later than last observation. Never skip a timestamp because identity/IoU is inconvenient. Unique same-class noncrowd GT IoU>=0.5, no interpolation. GT selects an evaluation reference only, never a runtime policy.",
  "readiness": "A clean query has unique reference identity, at least one uniquely own and one uniquely foreign available free candidate, each with>=3 frozen19-shift cells. Report and exclude from clean-readiness old references that already have another public native ID of the same unique GT, or targets already carried at current time by a non-newly-confirmed native track. Labels define diagnostic coverage, not runtime vetoes.",
  "gate": "At least3 clean queries across at least3 videos and at least1 query where the minimum existing native cost does NOT select only a uniquely own candidate. If gate fails, no map recovery or new similarity is justified by this inventory. Do not retune the gate to available cases.",
  "math": "A within-query comparison needs both true and foreign objects actually present in the candidate set. A wrong-only residual pool cannot test choosing the true object. For the frozen unclipped prediction-aligned reader, the same reference point has the same current query regardless of candidate; intersecting supports across all candidates therefore produces identical score grids. Do not propose that intersection as an identity discriminator; report native support separately.",
  "literature": "Mayer et al., KeepTrack, ICCV2021, https://arxiv.org/pdf/2103.16556, sections3 and4.1, official keep_track.py: joint candidate identities differ from a pooled similarity threshold. Already reviewed locally25Oct; no claim to implement KeepTrack or that it universally solves a sole candidate.",
